description=Solar power that behaves like solar power. Three grades of panel in ground and roof mounts, three grades of battery bank in floor and wall mounts, and banks that chain so a battery room can run right off the end of the controller's reach. Wire up whole buildings, carry power across town with transformers, and light your paths with solar lamps. Real solar geometry over Knox County: a flat roof panel wins July and loses January, an overcast sky costs you four fifths, and snow on the glass costs you all of it. Silent, unlike a generator, though you can convert a generator into a backup that only feeds your controller: it starts itself when the batteries run low, or runs by hand around the clock, and the monitor's GEN page shows it all. Panels and racks turn up in the world too: worn ones in garages, sheds, farm storage and electricians' vans, spare stock in hay barns, new stock on hardware and electronics shelves, and houses that already had a rig in the yard before all this. Find the county almanac and you can learn to read the sky: a reading gives you the next 29 days of weather as of the moment you took it, and the horizon shrinks a day per day until you read again.
